  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD023239",
    "title": "The proximal proteome of 17 SARS-CoV-2 proteins links to disrupted host antiviral signaling and translation",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "To study SARS-CoV-2 biology, we generated an atlas of 2422 human proteins vicinal to 17 SARS-CoV-2 viral proteins using proximity proteomics.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Perform BioID on 17 SARS-CoV-2 proteins to identify their binding proteins in the host proteome",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Maxquant, Version 1.5.2.8, was used to analyze the LC-MS and MS/MS data for protein identification and quantification.(Cox and Mann, 2008) The database we used for search was human IPI database, version 3.68, which contained 87,061 protein entries. The maximum number of miss-cleavages for trypsin was two per peptide.",
